```java
// For fields that must allow SOME HTML, use an allowlist sanitizer
import org.owasp.html.PolicyFactory;
import org.owasp.html.Sanitizers;

PolicyFactory policy = Sanitizers.FORMATTING.and(Sanitizers.LINKS);
String safeHtml = policy.sanitize(user.getBio());
// Keeps <b>, <i>, <a href>; strips <script>, onerror=, javascript: URLs
```

```java
// Only cleaning on input, then rendering raw -> still risky
String bio = sanitizeSomehow(request.getParameter("bio"));
userRepository.save(new User(bio));
```
```html
<!-- Rendering it raw assumes the sanitizer caught everything, in every context -->
<div th:utext="${user.bio}"></div>   <!-- one missed case = XSS -->
```
*Sanitization can miss context-specific payloads; rendering raw removes your safety net.*

```html
<!-- Default: encode on output, so plain-text fields are always safe -->
