```java
@Configuration
@EnableWebSecurity
public class SecurityConfig {

    @Bean
    SecurityFilterChain filterChain(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
        http.headers(headers -> headers
            .contentSecurityPolicy(csp -> csp
                // Only allow scripts/styles from our own origin; no inline script
                .policyDirectives(
                    "default-src 'self'; " +
                    "script-src 'self'; " +
                    "object-src 'none'; " +
                    "frame-ancestors 'none'")));
        return http.build();
    }
}
// Response header sent to every page:
//   Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; ...
// An injected <script>alert(1)</script> is blocked by the browser.
```
*Start in report-only mode (`Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only`) to find violations before enforcing.*
